I stand in front of a brightly lit snack stall.
I want to buy snacks for my colleagues at the software company.
"Give me a packet of banana chips," I say to the shopkeeper.
"I want a packet of jaggery-coated bananas too."
He takes two packets.
"How many rupees is it in total?" I ask.
The shopkeeper calculates the price.
"Sixty rupees for the chips," he says.
"Seventy rupees for the jaggery-coated bananas."
"One hundred and thirty rupees in total."
I open my purse.
I give him a five-hundred rupee note.
He takes that note.
He carefully counts the change.
"Here is the balance three hundred and seventy rupees," he says.
I take that money and the snacks.
This is for Prakash and the other colleagues.
